diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 02b1573..27c98b6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -46,15 +46,27 @@ moe-store convert deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat /ssd/stores/dsv2-lite
 moe-store inspect /ssd/stores/dsv2-lite
 ```

-Multimodal MoE checkpoints (Qwen3-VL-MoE, Qwen3-Omni-MoE) convert the same
+Multimodal MoE checkpoints (Qwen3-VL-MoE, Qwen3-Omni-MoE, Gemma4) convert the same
 way; resident towers (vision, audio, Omni talker) land in dense groups while
 the routed experts get one group per `(layer, expert)`:

 ```bash
 moe-store convert Qwen/Qwen3-VL-235B-A22B-Instruct /ssd/stores/qwen3-vl
 moe-store convert Qwen/Qwen3-Omni-30B-A3B-Instruct /ssd/stores/qwen3-omni
+moe-store convert google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it /ssd/stores/gemma4
 ```

+The experimental Gemma4 adapter targets the unquantized BF16
+`google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it` checkpoint. Conversion keeps its BF16 expert
+weights in gate/up/down slot order and leaves the router, dense MLP, and
+vision tower in dense groups. `SyncGemma4TextExperts` preserves the HF
+decoder's routing weights, including per-expert scales; it requires a
+MoE-Infinity runtime with the matching Gemma4 loader and GELU-tanh expert
+activation. The matching runtime passed tiny native GPU validation and two
+full 26B BF16 text/image greedy requests on A100, with output tokens matching
+the original HF model. This is a correctness smoke test; throughput and
+general accuracy were not measured.
+
 Dense diffusion transformers (diffusers-style `_class_name` configs) are
 stored as dense groups only. Single-component pipeline repos auto-descend
 into `transformer/`; roots with two or more weight-bearing components
